<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karaeng Matoaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1573–1636</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Sultan Abdullah of Tallo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karaeng Matoaya was ruler of Tallo and chancellor of the twin Makassar kingdom of Gowa. In 1605 he became the first Makassar ruler to accept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-khalji">Alauddin</a> of Gowa, and he guided the wars that forced Islam on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bugis">Bugis</a> states. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karaeng-pattingalloang">Karaeng Pattingalloang</a> was famed for his learning.</p></div>
